// ===========================================================================
// nightshade/tools/shot.hml — THE VISUAL VERIFICATION HARNESS  (W2-11, W3-0a)
// ===========================================================================
//
// This is not a debug utility. It is the primary quality instrument: the harsh
// visual critic runs it every iteration, and every art decision in the project
// is argued from its output.
//
//   hemlockc -O1 tools/shot.hml -o /tmp/shot
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene list
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene ridge_golden --out docs/shots/ridge_golden.png
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene atlas_sheet  --out docs/shots/atlas_sheet.png
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene muzzle_fog --cam 3,2.1,-8 --look 220,-4 \
//                                   --tod 22.0 --weather storm --seed 1337 --out /tmp/a.png
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --selftest
//
// THE SIX CONTRACTS (ARCHITECTURE.md §7, BUILD_PLAN W2-11 / W3-0a)
//
//  1. It renders through the REAL frame path — and since W3-0a that is no
//     longer a claim this file can make on its own behalf. `frame_render` now
//     lives in `src/render/world_render.hml`, imported below, shared with the
//     interactive walkaround, and enforced by `ci_imports.sh` R7: the moment
//     this file defines its own frame graph the build fails. This file drives
//     stages 6, 7 and 24 (time of day, the sky re-bake and its own HUD) and
//     the frame graph does 8..28. There is no second renderer here.
//  2. It renders the REAL ART. Every colour, tile, sprite, glyph, mesh, sky
//     row and lighting value in this file comes from `src/art/*` — palette,
//     tod, texgen, skygen, fxgen, hudgen, meshgen. There is no second art
//     pipeline in this file either, and there is no local copy of one.
//  3. Deterministic. No wall clock and no @stdlib/random reach any geometry
//     decision; every placement comes from `--seed` through the local xorshift
//     below, and `tod_reset()` clears the ToD crossfade/lightning state before
//     every evaluation. The same command produces byte-identical PNG bytes.
//  4. Compiled only. Run interpreted it refuses with a clear error and exit 2.
//  5. It never dies on a headless SDL failure — in particular
//     SDL_SetRelativeMouseMode always fails under SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy; that
//     is reported and rendering continues.
//  6. A screenshot without its stats report is impossible. The PNG and
//     `<out>.stats.txt` are written as a pair: if either write fails, neither
//     file survives, and the report is printed to stdout as well.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS FILE OWNS AND WHAT IT ONLY DRIVES
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OWNED (the harness): the CLI, the scene registry, the seeded test world
// (prop placement, particle placement, the built structures), determinism, the
// PNG+stats pairing, the compiled-only guard, the HUD, the stats plumbing,
// `--selftest`, and the `atlas_sheet` contact sheet.
//
// DRIVEN, NEVER REIMPLEMENTED (the frame graph): src/render/world_render.hml.
// The stage order, the layer order, the four batches, the LOD switch, the sky
// mapping and the readback are ITS. If a picture out of this tool is wrong in
// a way that would also be wrong while walking around, the fix belongs there.
//
// DRIVEN, NEVER REIMPLEMENTED (the art): palette.hml, tod.hml, texgen.hml,
// skygen.hml, fxgen.hml, hudgen.hml, meshgen.hml. If a picture out of this
// tool is ugly, the fix belongs in one of those seven files. That is the whole
// point: the harness must not be able to flatter or slander the art.
//
// The Wave-2 stand-in fence that used to sit here — a local palette, ToD
// table, texture generator, font and mesh set — is DELETED. It existed only
// because the art modules were being written in parallel with this file.
// ===========================================================================

